IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `aia-scope`
IMPORT `aia-definitions`
IMPORT `P2-section-2-gate`

-- P2-annex-iv: Annex IV (technical documentation referred to in Article 11(1)) of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act, Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744. The Omnibus did not change Annex IV.
-- Each point of the Annex is a function over the facts of that point; the chapeau ("shall contain at least the following information, as applicable to the relevant AI system") is the wrapper at the end, which takes the nine points' answers as a list and adds them up with the combinator of P2-section-2-gate.l4.
-- Every function takes the date asked, the AI system and the harmonisation facts and answers through the gate of Article 11(1) (the Article the Annex is referred to in): NOTHING when Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 do not apply to the system on the date asked,
-- JUST FALSE where Article 2(2) cuts it off, NOTHING where Article 2(13) says it may be limited. Reading a result: JUST TRUE the technical documentation contains what the point lists; JUST FALSE the text says no; NOTHING not covered.
-- Qualifiers inside a point ("where applicable", "where relevant", "as appropriate") are folded into that item's yes or no: answer yes where the qualifier makes the item inapplicable (fork F-qualifier-fold).
-- Seam S9: point 7 turns on whether harmonised standards were applied; whether a standard is a harmonised standard is the keel's `Art 3(27)`, called here.

§ `Annex IV, points 1 to 9`

-- src:1758 | 1. A general description of the AI system including:
-- src:1759 | (a) its intended purpose, the name of the provider and the version of the system reflecting its relation to previous versions;
-- src:1760 | (b) how the AI system interacts with, or can be used to interact with, hardware or software, including with other AI systems, that are not part of the AI system itself, where applicable;
-- src:1761 | (c) the versions of relevant software or firmware, and any requirements related to version updates;
-- src:1762 | (d) the description of all the forms in which the AI system is placed on the market or put into service, such as software packages embedded into hardware, downloads, or APIs;
-- src:1763 | (e) the description of the hardware on which the AI system is intended to run;
-- src:1764 | (f) where the AI system is a component of products, photographs or illustrations showing external features, the marking and internal layout of those products;
-- src:1765 | (g) a basic description of the user-interface provided to the deployer;
-- src:1766 | (h) instructions for use for the deployer, and a basic description of the user-interface provided to the deployer, where applicable;
@ref Annex IV point 1 (src:1758-1766)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the technical documentation contains a general description of the AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical documentation contains its intended purpose, the name of the provider and the version of the system reflecting its relation to previous versions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical documentation contains how the AI system interacts with, or can be used to interact with, hardware or software, including with other AI systems, that are not part of the AI system itself, where applicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical documentation contains the versions of relevant software or firmware, and any requirements related to version updates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical documentation contains the description of all the forms in which the AI system is placed on the market or put into service, such as software packages embedded into hardware, downloads, or APIs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical documentation contains the description of the hardware on which the AI system is intended to run` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical documentation contains where the AI system is a component of products, photographs or illustrations showing external features, the marking and internal layout of those products` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical documentation contains a basic description of the user-interface provided to the deployer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical documentation contains instructions for use for the deployer, and a basic description of the user-interface provided to the deployer, where applicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Annex IV point 1 the technical documentation contains a general description of the AI system` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 11, "", 1)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        JUST (`the technical documentation contains a general description of the AI system` AND `the technical documentation contains its intended purpose, the name of the provider and the version of the system reflecting its relation to previous versions` AND `the technical documentation contains how the AI system interacts with, or can be used to interact with, hardware or software, including with other AI systems, that are not part of the AI system itself, where applicable` AND `the technical documentation contains the versions of relevant software or firmware, and any requirements related to version updates` AND `the technical documentation contains the description of all the forms in which the AI system is placed on the market or put into service, such as software packages embedded into hardware, downloads, or APIs` AND `the technical documentation contains the description of the hardware on which the AI system is intended to run` AND `the technical documentation contains where the AI system is a component of products, photographs or illustrations showing external features, the marking and internal layout of those products` AND `the technical documentation contains a basic description of the user-interface provided to the deployer` AND `the technical documentation contains instructions for use for the deployer, and a basic description of the user-interface provided to the deployer, where applicable`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A general description of the AI system including:"
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed

-- src:1767 | 2. A detailed description of the elements of the AI system and of the process for its development, including:
-- src:1768 | (a) the methods and steps performed for the development of the AI system, including, where relevant, recourse to pre-trained systems or tools provided by third parties and how those were used, integrated or modified by the provider;
-- src:1769 | (b) the design specifications of the system, namely the general logic of the AI system and of the algorithms; the key design choices including the rationale and assumptions made, including with regard to persons or groups of persons in respect of who, the system is intended to be used; the main classification choices; what the system is designed to optimise for, and the relevance of the different parameters; the description of the expected output and output quality of the system; the decisions about any possible trade-off made regarding the technical solutions adopted to comply with the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2;
-- src:1770 | (c) the description of the system architecture explaining how software components build on or feed into each other and integrate into the overall processing; the computational resources used to develop, train, test and validate the AI system;
-- src:1771 | (d) where relevant, the data requirements in terms of datasheets describing the training methodologies and techniques and the training data sets used, including a general description of these data sets, information about their provenance, scope and main characteristics; how the data was obtained and selected; labelling procedures (e.g. for supervised learning), data cleaning methodologies (e.g. outliers detection);
-- src:1772 | (e) assessment of the human oversight measures needed in accordance with Article 14, including an assessment of the technical measures needed to facilitate the interpretation of the outputs of AI systems by the deployers, in accordance with Article 13(3), point (d);
-- src:1773 | (f) where applicable, a detailed description of pre-determined changes to the AI system and its performance, together with all the relevant information related to the technical solutions adopted to ensure continuous compliance of the AI system with the relevant requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2;
-- src:1774 | (g) the validation and testing procedures used, including information about the validation and testing data used and their main characteristics; metrics used to measure accuracy, robustness and compliance with other relevant requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2, as well as potentially discriminatory impacts; test logs and all test reports dated and signed by the responsible persons, including with regard to pre-determined changes as referred to under point (f);
-- src:1775 | (h) cybersecurity measures put in place;
@ref Annex IV point 2 (src:1767-1775)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the technical documentation contains a detailed description of the elements of the AI system and of the process for its development` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical documentation contains the methods and steps performed for the development of the AI system, including, where relevant, recourse to pre-trained systems or tools provided by third parties and how those were used, integrated or modified by the provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical documentation contains the design specifications of the system, namely the general logic of the AI system and of the algorithms` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical documentation contains the key design choices including the rationale and assumptions made, including with regard to persons or groups of persons in respect of who the system is intended to be used` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical documentation contains the main classification choices` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical documentation contains what the system is designed to optimise for, and the relevance of the different parameters` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical documentation contains the description of the expected output and output quality of the system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical documentation contains the decisions about any possible trade-off made regarding the technical solutions adopted to comply with the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical documentation contains the description of the system architecture explaining how software components build on or feed into each other and integrate into the overall processing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical documentation contains the computational resources used to develop, train, test and validate the AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical documentation contains where relevant, the data requirements in terms of datasheets describing the training methodologies and techniques and the training data sets used, including a general description of these data sets, information about their provenance, scope and main characteristics; how the data was obtained and selected; labelling procedures (e.g. for supervised learning), data cleaning methodologies (e.g. outliers detection)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical documentation contains an assessment of the human oversight measures needed in accordance with Article 14, including an assessment of the technical measures needed to facilitate the interpretation of the outputs of AI systems by the deployers, in accordance with Article 13(3), point (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical documentation contains where applicable, a detailed description of pre-determined changes to the AI system and its performance, together with all the relevant information related to the technical solutions adopted to ensure continuous compliance of the AI system with the relevant requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical documentation contains the validation and testing procedures used, including information about the validation and testing data used and their main characteristics` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical documentation contains the metrics used to measure accuracy, robustness and compliance with other relevant requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2, as well as potentially discriminatory impacts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical documentation contains test logs and all test reports dated and signed by the responsible persons, including with regard to pre-determined changes as referred to under point (f)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical documentation contains cybersecurity measures put in place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Annex IV point 2 the technical documentation contains a detailed description of the elements of the AI system and of the process for its development` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 11, "", 1)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        JUST (`the technical documentation contains a detailed description of the elements of the AI system and of the process for its development` AND `the technical documentation contains the methods and steps performed for the development of the AI system, including, where relevant, recourse to pre-trained systems or tools provided by third parties and how those were used, integrated or modified by the provider` AND `the technical documentation contains the design specifications of the system, namely the general logic of the AI system and of the algorithms` AND `the technical documentation contains the key design choices including the rationale and assumptions made, including with regard to persons or groups of persons in respect of who the system is intended to be used` AND `the technical documentation contains the main classification choices` AND `the technical documentation contains what the system is designed to optimise for, and the relevance of the different parameters` AND `the technical documentation contains the description of the expected output and output quality of the system` AND `the technical documentation contains the decisions about any possible trade-off made regarding the technical solutions adopted to comply with the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2` AND `the technical documentation contains the description of the system architecture explaining how software components build on or feed into each other and integrate into the overall processing` AND `the technical documentation contains the computational resources used to develop, train, test and validate the AI system` AND `the technical documentation contains where relevant, the data requirements in terms of datasheets describing the training methodologies and techniques and the training data sets used, including a general description of these data sets, information about their provenance, scope and main characteristics; how the data was obtained and selected; labelling procedures (e.g. for supervised learning), data cleaning methodologies (e.g. outliers detection)` AND `the technical documentation contains an assessment of the human oversight measures needed in accordance with Article 14, including an assessment of the technical measures needed to facilitate the interpretation of the outputs of AI systems by the deployers, in accordance with Article 13(3), point (d)` AND `the technical documentation contains where applicable, a detailed description of pre-determined changes to the AI system and its performance, together with all the relevant information related to the technical solutions adopted to ensure continuous compliance of the AI system with the relevant requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2` AND `the technical documentation contains the validation and testing procedures used, including information about the validation and testing data used and their main characteristics` AND `the technical documentation contains the metrics used to measure accuracy, robustness and compliance with other relevant requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2, as well as potentially discriminatory impacts` AND `the technical documentation contains test logs and all test reports dated and signed by the responsible persons, including with regard to pre-determined changes as referred to under point (f)` AND `the technical documentation contains cybersecurity measures put in place`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A detailed description of the elements of the AI system and of the process for its development, including:"
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed

-- src:1776 | 3. Detailed information about the monitoring, functioning and control of the AI system, in particular with regard to: its capabilities and limitations in performance, including the degrees of accuracy for specific persons or groups of persons on which the system is intended to be used and the overall expected level of accuracy in relation to its intended purpose; the foreseeable unintended outcomes and sources of risks to health and safety, fundamental rights and discrimination in view of the intended purpose of the AI system; the human oversight measures needed in accordance with Article 14, including the technical measures put in place to facilitate the interpretation of the outputs of AI systems by the deployers; specifications on input data, as appropriate;
@ref Annex IV point 3 (src:1776)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the technical documentation contains detailed information about the monitoring, functioning and control of the AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical documentation contains its capabilities and limitations in performance, including the degrees of accuracy for specific persons or groups of persons on which the system is intended to be used and the overall expected level of accuracy in relation to its intended purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical documentation contains the foreseeable unintended outcomes and sources of risks to health and safety, fundamental rights and discrimination in view of the intended purpose of the AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical documentation contains the human oversight measures needed in accordance with Article 14, including the technical measures put in place to facilitate the interpretation of the outputs of AI systems by the deployers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical documentation contains specifications on input data, as appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Annex IV point 3 the technical documentation contains detailed information about the monitoring, functioning and control of the AI system` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 11, "", 1)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        JUST (`the technical documentation contains detailed information about the monitoring, functioning and control of the AI system` AND `the technical documentation contains its capabilities and limitations in performance, including the degrees of accuracy for specific persons or groups of persons on which the system is intended to be used and the overall expected level of accuracy in relation to its intended purpose` AND `the technical documentation contains the foreseeable unintended outcomes and sources of risks to health and safety, fundamental rights and discrimination in view of the intended purpose of the AI system` AND `the technical documentation contains the human oversight measures needed in accordance with Article 14, including the technical measures put in place to facilitate the interpretation of the outputs of AI systems by the deployers` AND `the technical documentation contains specifications on input data, as appropriate`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Detailed information about the monitoring, functioning and control of the AI system, in particular with regard to:"
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed

-- src:1777 | 4. A description of the appropriateness of the performance metrics for the specific AI system;
@ref Annex IV point 4 (src:1777)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the technical documentation contains a description of the appropriateness of the performance metrics for the specific AI system` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Annex IV point 4 the technical documentation contains a description of the appropriateness of the performance metrics` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 11, "", 1)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        JUST (`the technical documentation contains a description of the appropriateness of the performance metrics for the specific AI system`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A description of the appropriateness of the performance metrics for the specific AI system"
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed

