      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the technical documentation contains a detailed description of the risk management system in accordance with Article 9` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Annex IV point 5 the technical documentation contains a detailed description of the risk management system` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 11, "", 1)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        JUST (`the technical documentation contains a detailed description of the risk management system in accordance with Article 9`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A detailed description of the risk management system in accordance with Article 9"
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed

-- src:1779 | 6. A description of relevant changes made by the provider to the system through its lifecycle;
@ref Annex IV point 6 (src:1779)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the technical documentation contains a description of relevant changes made by the provider to the system through its lifecycle` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Annex IV point 6 the technical documentation contains a description of relevant changes made by the provider to the system` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 11, "", 1)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        JUST (`the technical documentation contains a description of relevant changes made by the provider to the system through its lifecycle`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A description of relevant changes made by the provider to the system through its lifecycle"
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed

-- src:1780 | 7. A list of the harmonised standards applied in full or in part the references of which have been published in the Official Journal of the European Union; where no such harmonised standards have been applied, a detailed description of the solutions adopted to meet the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2, including a list of other relevant standards and technical specifications applied;
@ref Annex IV point 7 (src:1780)
-- Seam S9: whether a standard is a harmonised standard is the keel's `Art 3(27)` (a borrowed fact). The point is a disjunction by cases: with such standards applied, the list; where none, the description.
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the standard applied is a harmonised standard as defined in Article 2(1), point (c), of Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the references of the standard applied have been published in the Official Journal of the European Union` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the standard has been applied in full or in part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical documentation contains a list of the harmonised standards applied in full or in part the references of which have been published in the Official Journal of the European Union` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical documentation contains where no such harmonised standards have been applied, a detailed description of the solutions adopted to meet the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2, including a list of other relevant standards and technical specifications applied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Annex IV point 7 the technical documentation contains a list of the harmonised standards applied or a description of the solutions adopted` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 11, "", 1)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        JUST (IF (`Art 3(27) the standard is a harmonised standard` `the standard applied is a harmonised standard as defined in Article 2(1), point (c), of Regulation (EU) No 1025/2012`) AND `the references of the standard applied have been published in the Official Journal of the European Union` AND `the standard has been applied in full or in part` THEN `the technical documentation contains a list of the harmonised standards applied in full or in part the references of which have been published in the Official Journal of the European Union` ELSE `the technical documentation contains where no such harmonised standards have been applied, a detailed description of the solutions adopted to meet the requirements set out in Chapter III, Section 2, including a list of other relevant standards and technical specifications applied`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A list of the harmonised standards applied in full or in part ...; where no such harmonised standards have been applied, a detailed description of the solutions adopted"
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed

-- src:1781 | 8. A copy of the EU declaration of conformity referred to in Article 47;
@ref Annex IV point 8 (src:1781)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the technical documentation contains a copy of the EU declaration of conformity referred to in Article 47` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Annex IV point 8 the technical documentation contains a copy of the EU declaration of conformity` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 11, "", 1)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        JUST (`the technical documentation contains a copy of the EU declaration of conformity referred to in Article 47`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A copy of the EU declaration of conformity referred to in Article 47"
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed

-- src:1782 | 9. A detailed description of the system in place to evaluate the AI system performance in the post-market phase in accordance with Article 72, including the post-market monitoring plan referred to in Article 72(3).
@ref Annex IV point 9 (src:1782)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the technical documentation contains a detailed description of the system in place to evaluate the AI system performance in the post-market phase in accordance with Article 72` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the technical documentation contains the post-market monitoring plan referred to in Article 72(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Annex IV point 9 the technical documentation contains a detailed description of the post-market evaluation system and the monitoring plan` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 11, "", 1)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        JUST (`the technical documentation contains a detailed description of the system in place to evaluate the AI system performance in the post-market phase in accordance with Article 72` AND `the technical documentation contains the post-market monitoring plan referred to in Article 72(3)`)  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A detailed description of the system in place to evaluate the AI system performance in the post-market phase in accordance with Article 72, including the post-market monitoring plan referred to in Article 72(3)"
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" to a high-risk AI system under Article 6(1) related to Section B products (seam S14, the keel's answer)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of this requirement "may be limited"; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed


§ `Annex IV, the chapeau`

-- src:1757 | The technical documentation referred to in Article 11(1) shall contain at least the following information, as applicable to the relevant AI system:
@ref Annex IV chapeau (src:1757)
-- The chapeau: the technical documentation "shall contain at least the following information, as applicable to the relevant AI system". The nine points' answers come in as a list; one point not contained is the text's own no.
-- "as applicable to the relevant AI system" is carried by each point's own qualifiers (folded into each item's yes or no).
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the harmonisation facts` IS A `Arts 8 to 15 harmonisation facts`
      `the answers of points 1 to 9 of Annex IV` IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Annex IV the technical documentation contains at least the following information` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Arts 8 to 15 the gate for the requirement` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the harmonisation facts` (`Article reference` OF 11, "", 1)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate the requirement applies` THEN
        `Arts 8 to 15 all the requirements are met given the answers` `the answers of points 1 to 9 of Annex IV`  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall contain at least the following information": a point not contained is the no; NOTHING where no point is answered
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate cut off by Article 2(2)` THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): Article 2(2) "only Article 6(1), Article 60a and Articles 102 to 112 shall apply" (seam S14)
    WHEN `Arts 8 to 15 gate may be limited under Article 2(13)` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Article 2(13) says the application of Article 11 may be limited; how far is for the delegated acts it names
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Chapter III Section 2 applies from the date Article 113(c) gives, and Article 111(2) saves a system placed earlier and not significantly changed
